WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

2
00:01:03.049 --> 00:01:04.175
Yes. Mr. Cho.

3
00:01:05.009 --> 00:01:06.511
Yes. that's the place.

4
00:01:11.269 --> 00:01:15.023
The warehouse where we
worked on the Japanese kid.

5
00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:19.857
Yes. he's comfy and well.

6
00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:23.068
He was a lot gentler than what you told me.

7
00:01:25.569 --> 00:01:29.490
He wasn't trouble at all.
he took my lead well.

8
00:01:30.329 --> 00:01:32.289
He was a bit cheeky though.

9
00:01:33.249 --> 00:01:35.418
He's a funny guy.

10
00:01:39.959 --> 00:01:44.046
How much was this guy worth by the way?

11
00:01:51.219 --> 00:01:54.848
Right? I knew he was loaded.

12
00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:58.393
He's covered in designer goods.

13
00:02:00.819 --> 00:02:01.820
What?

14
00:02:03.949 --> 00:02:05.159
Oh...

15
00:02:07.319 --> 00:02:09.863
He must be rich.

16
00:02:13.289 --> 00:02:14.749
Yes. I see.

17
00:02:14.749 --> 00:02:17.960
We got a proper merchandise for once.

18
00:02:22.089 --> 00:02:25.634
Almost here? I left the door open.

19
00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:27.052
Come on right in.

20
00:02:28.089 --> 00:02:29.299
I'll see...

21
00:02:30.969 --> 00:02:33.430
Fucker. I was talking...

22
00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:35.348
Mr. Cho's almost here.

23
00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:24.154
Get out!

24
00:03:24.399 --> 00:03:25.400
Get out now!

25
00:03:52.509 --> 00:03:54.011
Shit!

26
00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:00.525
Fuck...

27
00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:22.540
It's been a while. friend.

28
00:04:25.629 --> 00:04:28.674
I told you. you'd see me again soon.

29
00:04:29.719 --> 00:04:31.137
You... wait...

30
00:04:32.089 --> 00:04:34.300
It's just...

31
00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.886
Oh yeah. I said I'd give you money.

32
00:04:37.886 --> 00:04:40.639
I'll give it to you for real!

33
00:04:40.639 --> 00:04:43.434
I'm not lying this time.
you'll get it. okay?

34
00:04:49.359 --> 00:04:50.527
It's fine.

35
00:04:51.279 --> 00:04:53.490
Friends shouldn't pay each other money.

36
00:05:11.589 --> 00:05:14.008
Don't kill me! Please don't kill me!

37
00:05:14.008 --> 00:05:16.552
Goddammit. what are you doing?!
You got blood on my shoe!

38
00:05:16.552 --> 00:05:17.637
Motherfucker!

39
00:05:22.519 --> 00:05:25.605
Asshole.
it's this season's brand new model!

40
00:05:25.609 --> 00:05:27.611
I barely managed to buy it
from the first batch!

41
00:05:28.689 --> 00:05:31.567
I could just fucking kill you!

42
00:05:52.669 --> 00:05:53.753
Look at it.

43
00:05:56.179 --> 00:06:01.226
I'm going to use this
to carve your heart out.

44
00:06:02.269 --> 00:06:03.604
You know what?

45
00:06:03.604 --> 00:06:09.359
Blunt instruments are more painful
than sharp knives.

46
00:06:09.359 --> 00:06:11.361
You can't die quickly with these.

47
00:06:11.361 --> 00:06:13.906
How much is your client paying you?

48
00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.824
I'll pay you double...

49
00:06:22.619 --> 00:06:25.080
Friend. you said we're friends!

50
00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:26.540
Don't kill me. please!

51
00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:27.791
Right. friend.

52
00:06:28.379 --> 00:06:29.714
I told you.

53
00:06:31.799 --> 00:06:37.138
I'm the last friend you'll meet

54
00:06:37.138 --> 00:06:38.764
before you die.

55
00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:41.884
It's nothing personal.

56
00:06:41.884 --> 00:06:44.345
We're pros. and this is just business.

57
00:06:56.859 --> 00:07:02.948
THE CHILDE

58
00:07:05.369 --> 00:07:07.830
Executive Producer KIM WOO-TAEK

59
00:07:08.829 --> 00:07:11.290
Produced by PARK HOON-JUNG

60
00:07:43.449 --> 00:07:45.910
Written & Directed by PARK HOON-JUNG

61
00:08:26.619 --> 00:08:27.912
Nice work today. Marco.

62
00:08:46.559 --> 00:08:48.811
You promised me more
from this match onwards.

63
00:08:55.319 --> 00:08:56.320
Hey. Marco!

64
00:08:56.819 --> 00:08:59.530
You eat well and take care
of yourself with that money!

65
00:08:59.899 --> 00:09:01.859
You know about the big match
next week. right?

66
00:09:02.239 --> 00:09:03.949
I put a shit load of money on you!

67
00:09:04.909 --> 00:09:06.160
Arrogant bastard...

68
00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:07.954
Fucking Kopino half-breed...!

69
00:10:44.219 --> 00:10:47.097
Got your butt kicked this time?

70
00:10:49.889 --> 00:10:52.100
Your opponent was a Thai?

71
00:10:55.479 --> 00:11:01.110
Those Thais sure got spicy punches.

72
00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:05.322
Someone really did a number
on our mighty Marco's face.

73
00:11:07.699 --> 00:11:10.285
Don't glare at me. idiot.

74
00:11:10.285 --> 00:11:12.621
How's your mother?

75
00:11:17.039 --> 00:11:19.500
She should really get that surgery soon.

76
00:11:20.589 --> 00:11:22.049
What brings you here today?

77
00:11:22.919 --> 00:11:24.295
Because of your father?

78
00:11:26.919 --> 00:11:28.045
Any news?

79
00:11:30.009 --> 00:11:33.721
Nothing so far.

80
00:11:35.349 --> 00:11:37.142
But hang in there.

81
00:11:37.142 --> 00:11:40.271
If he's alive. you might find him one day.

82
00:11:40.689 --> 00:11:43.192
I wouldn't even be looking for that man

83
00:11:43.192 --> 00:11:45.360
if it wasn't for Mom's operation.

84
00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:48.071
Come on now.

85
00:11:51.949 --> 00:11:52.950
What's that?

86
00:11:55.289 --> 00:11:57.500
Use it to hire someone in
Korea to look for him.

87
00:11:58.369 --> 00:12:00.454
Hey! Hey!

88
00:12:01.249 --> 00:12:03.626
Marco!

89
00:12:22.059 --> 00:12:23.727
You're later than usual.

90
00:12:24.109 --> 00:12:26.695
LaLiga's it's closed already

91
00:12:26.695 --> 00:12:29.865
but Premier League is still betting.

92
00:12:31.069 --> 00:12:32.737
Which team has the highest odds?

93
00:12:33.949 --> 00:12:35.868
Let's see...

94
00:12:38.159 --> 00:12:39.160
Um. Burnley?

95
00:12:39.499 --> 00:12:41.376
Yeah. it's Burnley.

96
00:12:41.619 --> 00:12:43.079
They're going against Chelsea.

97
00:12:43.629 --> 00:12:44.797
What are the odds?

98
00:12:45.419 --> 00:12:47.421
250 to 1.

99
00:12:49.879 --> 00:12:50.880
All on Burnley.

100
00:12:51.839 --> 00:12:52.840
Hey Marco.

101
00:12:53.259 --> 00:12:54.761
that's not a great idea.

102
00:12:54.929 --> 00:12:56.889
Why don't you just buy the lotto ticket?

103
00:12:57.009 --> 00:12:58.677
You a lot of better chance at winning.

104
00:12:59.269 --> 00:13:01.229
I said all on Burnley.

105
00:13:02.479 --> 00:13:04.022
Whatever.

106
00:13:16.159 --> 00:13:17.160
It's on me. mate.

107
00:13:18.039 --> 00:13:19.457
Long time no see. Marco.

108
00:13:19.699 --> 00:13:23.036
That last fight was fucking sick. huh?

109
00:13:23.539 --> 00:13:25.916
Big shot Thai guy didn't
fucking stand a chance.

110
00:13:26.339 --> 00:13:28.967
Thanks to you... I made a pretty penny.

111
00:13:29.549 --> 00:13:30.675
Um? thanks for that...

112
00:13:32.129 --> 00:13:33.213
Oh yeah. So ah...

113
00:13:34.049 --> 00:13:35.342
how's searching for daddy going?

114
00:13:35.599 --> 00:13:36.600
Any leads?

115
00:13:41.099 --> 00:13:42.225
Of course not...

116
00:13:42.519 --> 00:13:43.520
What do you care?

117
00:13:46.979 --> 00:13:49.315
But I do have a job that
might interest you.

118
00:13:51.149 --> 00:13:54.569
I've had my eye on this
fancy jewelry store downtown.

119
00:13:54.989 --> 00:13:58.326
I'm gonna get to work on it... You want in?

120
00:13:59.739 --> 00:14:01.157
Come on. man.

121
00:14:01.539 --> 00:14:03.666
All you have to do is cut the power

122
00:14:03.669 --> 00:14:04.879
and keep the security busy.

123
00:14:05.249 --> 00:14:07.418
You don't even have to go in
and I'll give you 10%.

124
00:14:07.999 --> 00:14:09.584
Store that size...

125
00:14:09.999 --> 00:14:13.044
even with the middleman
it'll be 100 big ones. easy.

126
00:14:15.799 --> 00:14:16.925
10% Marco...

127
00:14:17.389 --> 00:14:18.390
What do you say?

128
00:14:19.849 --> 00:14:20.600
I'll think about it.

129
00:14:20.809 --> 00:14:22.728
Come on. man. Fuck!

130
00:14:22.729 --> 00:14:23.855
What's there to think about?

131
00:14:24.639 --> 00:14:25.765
You know what.

132
00:14:26.519 --> 00:14:29.022
I'll even forget about mommy's medication.

133
00:14:55.049 --> 00:14:58.219
Chelsea 4:0

134
00:15:14.319 --> 00:15:17.614
Yo. Chelsea took all your money.

135
00:15:26.709 --> 00:15:28.586
When you go around the back to the building

136
00:15:28.586 --> 00:15:31.631
you'll find the power box
and a guard booth.

137
00:15:32.839 --> 00:15:33.840
Here.

138
00:15:36.919 --> 00:15:38.587
They'll bust in as soon as you

139
00:15:38.587 --> 00:15:39.547
keep the guards to busy.

140
00:15:39.547 --> 00:15:40.714
cut the power to the building.

141
00:15:41.219 --> 00:15:42.470
No problem.

142
00:17:07.719 --> 00:17:08.970
Get back fuckers!

143
00:17:52.389 --> 00:17:54.433
Hey! Are you okay?!

144
00:17:57.149 --> 00:18:01.153
Oh no. are you okay?
I didn't see you run out...

145
00:18:03.029 --> 00:18:05.448
We should go to the hospital...

146
00:18:06.069 --> 00:18:07.988
Why am I speaking Korean?

147
00:18:09.159 --> 00:18:10.369
I'm really sorry.

148
00:18:10.449 --> 00:18:12.326
We should go to a hospital right away.

149
00:18:13.869 --> 00:18:14.953
Korean?

150
00:18:16.329 --> 00:18:18.373
- Are you Korean? - What?

151
00:18:20.879 --> 00:18:22.881
Well. not exactly.

152
00:19:06.929 --> 00:19:09.140
How are you feeling?

153
00:19:09.799 --> 00:19:12.135
All the tests came back well.

154
00:19:12.135 --> 00:19:14.554
I told you this was unnecessary.

155
00:19:14.554 --> 00:19:17.098
we could've settled last night.
what was the point of this?

156
00:19:17.098 --> 00:19:20.560
Even so. you just never know
with accidents.

157
00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:22.478
There could be lasting effects.

158
00:19:25.649 --> 00:19:29.027
This isn't much. please take it.
and I'm so sorry.

159
00:19:33.159 --> 00:19:37.580
By the way. you speak Korean really well.

160
00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:39.123
You look like one too.

161
00:19:39.129 --> 00:19:41.506
anyone will think that you're a Korean.

162
00:19:42.749 --> 00:19:44.334
I get that a lot.

163
00:19:44.334 --> 00:19:46.878
Did you learn Korean somewhere?

164
00:19:49.469 --> 00:19:51.054
Or are you...

165
00:19:51.054 --> 00:19:53.139
what was it called?

166
00:19:53.139 --> 00:19:54.140
Kopino?

167
00:19:55.019 --> 00:19:56.270
You are Kopino. right?

168
00:20:01.019 --> 00:20:02.896
Sorry. I shouldn't have said that...

169
00:20:28.549 --> 00:20:29.550
Yeah?

170
00:20:32.929 --> 00:20:33.930
What?

171
00:20:45.899 --> 00:20:49.111
I was gonna take your money.

172
00:20:49.111 --> 00:20:51.488
but it stank so badly of your sweat.

173
00:20:54.829 --> 00:20:58.958
It'd be proper to say that
they were looking for us.

174
00:20:58.959 --> 00:21:01.879
rather than us looking for them.

175
00:21:03.249 --> 00:21:07.587
It means your father
did not forget about you.

176
00:21:07.587 --> 00:21:11.007
As you know. cases like this are so rare.

177
00:21:11.007 --> 00:21:15.928
How many fathers came looking
for their Kopino kids here?

178
00:21:15.928 --> 00:21:17.513
None. zero.

179
00:21:17.519 --> 00:21:21.648
They just plant their seeds
and get the hell out of here.

180
00:21:22.689 --> 00:21:24.399
When is he coming?

181
00:21:24.399 --> 00:21:26.943
Oh yeah. he's coming right away.

182
00:21:26.943 --> 00:21:28.612
It looked like he was in a hurry.

183
00:21:30.359 --> 00:21:33.320
And this is my gift to you.

184
00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:34.989
It's a Korean calling card.

185
00:21:34.989 --> 00:21:38.826
You might need it there.
so keep it with you.

186
00:22:08.609 --> 00:22:10.111
What a stench.

187
00:22:51.689 --> 00:22:52.773
Marco Han?

188
00:22:55.909 --> 00:22:57.119
You're him.

189
00:22:58.909 --> 00:22:59.910
Good to meet you.

190
00:23:15.339 --> 00:23:16.757
Thank you.

191
00:23:31.939 --> 00:23:33.315
Law Firm The Royal Partner Kang Won-seok

192
00:23:33.315 --> 00:23:36.277
Your father's a bit sick.

193
00:23:36.277 --> 00:23:38.237
so I came instead.

194
00:23:39.119 --> 00:23:41.580
Do you understand what I just said?

195
00:23:42.699 --> 00:23:46.077
I don't speak Tagalog at all.

196
00:23:46.077 --> 00:23:47.829
but a little English.
would you prefer that?

197
00:23:49.999 --> 00:23:52.043
It's okay. you can speak Korean.

198
00:23:54.049 --> 00:23:56.510
You speak Korean so well.

199
00:23:56.510 --> 00:23:59.346
Mom forced me to speak Korean or English.

200
00:24:00.089 --> 00:24:01.632
I had to go to a Korean school.

201
00:24:01.632 --> 00:24:03.092
Korean school?

202
00:24:22.659 --> 00:24:25.120
You need those to fly.

203
00:24:25.829 --> 00:24:27.998
Passport. visa and such.

204
00:24:29.079 --> 00:24:32.708
Isn't money great?
Anything is solvable with it.

205
00:24:36.049 --> 00:24:38.051
Han. look here.

206
00:24:38.051 --> 00:24:41.054
She's a hospice nurse who
will look after your mother.

207
00:24:41.054 --> 00:24:44.766
Because of your father's condition.
we have to hurry.

208
00:24:44.766 --> 00:24:46.851
Pack lightly and come out.

209
00:24:49.099 --> 00:24:50.601
Right now?

210
00:24:50.601 --> 00:24:52.477
Why? ls there a problem?

211
00:24:53.149 --> 00:24:54.150
But...

212
00:24:58.989 --> 00:25:03.285
For her sake.
wouldn't it be best to head out ASAP?

213
00:25:03.285 --> 00:25:08.123
Paying for her surgery is not
even a bother to him.

214
00:25:08.123 --> 00:25:10.167
He'll take care of it right away.

215
00:25:11.579 --> 00:25:13.748
It's a quick flight to Seoul.

216
00:25:13.748 --> 00:25:16.250
Pack up quickly. okay?

217
00:25:16.250 --> 00:25:18.211
He really wants to see you.

218
00:25:30.599 --> 00:25:32.309
Hokyung Foundation Accused of Slush Fund...

219
00:25:33.309 --> 00:25:36.187
Illegal Succession at Hokyung Foundation...

220
00:25:36.187 --> 00:25:38.397
Hokyung Foundation's Slush Fund
Whistleblowers Missing...

221
00:25:48.539 --> 00:25:51.042
Attorney Kang Won-seok

222
00:26:07.179 --> 00:26:10.182
Yes. Kang. how did it go?

223
00:26:11.979 --> 00:26:15.191
Very good. that's great.

224
00:26:17.979 --> 00:26:19.147
When's the flight?

225
00:26:23.149 --> 00:26:24.275
Okay.

226
00:26:25.909 --> 00:26:30.288
I'll have everyone on standby.
come here at once.

227
00:26:32.459 --> 00:26:34.378
Okay. good.

228
00:26:41.879 --> 00:26:43.547
So? How did it go?

229
00:26:43.547 --> 00:26:44.548
Sir?

230
00:26:45.589 --> 00:26:50.219
Thankfully.
their editors are quite amicable to us.

231
00:26:50.219 --> 00:26:51.970
so we managed to kill all articles.

232
00:26:51.970 --> 00:26:52.930
Return for what?

233
00:26:52.930 --> 00:26:57.101
We will be the main sponsor
for Daeil Daily's annual

234
00:26:57.101 --> 00:26:59.853
corporation expo for the next <i>3</i> years.

235
00:26:59.853 --> 00:27:02.106
For the other 3 outlets.
we'll be the main ad client...

236
00:27:02.106 --> 00:27:03.690
So pathetic...

237
00:27:06.199 --> 00:27:09.494
It's so easy taking someone else's money.

238
00:27:10.159 --> 00:27:11.952
It's a sensitive period.

239
00:27:11.952 --> 00:27:16.082
it'd be best not to get mixed up
with malicious tabloids.

240
00:27:16.829 --> 00:27:17.955
I know.

241
00:27:19.419 --> 00:27:22.380
Do I look like a moron
who can't read the room?

242
00:27:22.380 --> 00:27:24.424
That's not what I meant.

243
00:27:24.424 --> 00:27:25.592
Whatever.

244
00:27:26.299 --> 00:27:27.300
Sir?

245
00:27:27.300 --> 00:27:29.010
That'll be all.

246
00:27:29.010 --> 00:27:30.011
Yes. sir.

247
00:27:34.179 --> 00:27:36.640
You haven't been here in a long time.

248
00:27:36.640 --> 00:27:39.393
Get some rest and see you tomorrow.

249
00:27:39.393 --> 00:27:42.979
That's all right. sir.
I'll head back to Seoul...

250
00:27:44.739 --> 00:27:46.407
As you wish. sir.

251
00:27:46.407 --> 00:27:48.576
There's someone I want you to meet.

252
00:27:49.569 --> 00:27:51.279
so let's have breakfast tomorrow.

253
00:27:51.279 --> 00:27:52.280
Yes. sir.

254
00:27:54.119 --> 00:27:55.120
This way.

255
00:28:13.309 --> 00:28:17.355
So. Father. how are you holding up?

256
00:28:22.399 --> 00:28:25.360
They're leaving the Philippines.
so just hang in there.

257
00:28:28.909 --> 00:28:29.910
What did you say?

258
00:28:33.239 --> 00:28:37.285
Yes. Father. the youngest.

259
00:28:37.285 --> 00:28:40.830
That youngest son you've been
waiting for is on the way.

260
00:28:41.879 --> 00:28:42.963
Happy?

261
00:28:46.169 --> 00:28:47.170
Are you?

262
00:28:51.219 --> 00:28:54.472
Yes. that mutt.

263
00:29:00.019 --> 00:29:02.104
Your mutt's on the way here.

264
00:29:03.519 --> 00:29:07.523
Just hang on until he arrives. okay?

265
00:29:15.199 --> 00:29:16.701
We don't have time.

266
00:29:16.701 --> 00:29:19.870
Have cars on standby so that
we can leave immediately.

267
00:29:19.870 --> 00:29:21.038
Understood. sir.

268
00:30:31.899 --> 00:30:34.819
Man. I almost missed it.

269
00:30:34.819 --> 00:30:39.198
I thought you'd leave tomorrow.
but returning on the same day?

270
00:30:39.198 --> 00:30:41.325
They must really be in a hurry.

271
00:30:42.499 --> 00:30:45.669
They're filthy rich.
